        helpPresentTitle: "Presenting to a room",
        helpPresentIntro: "Present puts a large date banner on the map with its own play buttons, so the audience watches the map and not the panel.",
        helpPresent1: "Press Present. The slider switches to As of and moves to the first chapter, or the oldest date, when it was sitting at the end. The banner opens on a title card, then shows the date, a progress bar and the current chapter, and a closing card at the end. Full screen, or F, fills the screen with the map. Press Exit presentation, or Escape, to come back; the mode you were in comes back with you.",
        helpPresentKeys: "Space plays and pauses. The arrow keys step one notch. Home and End go to either end. Shift with an arrow, or Page Up and Page Down, moves a chapter. Type a chapter number and press Enter to jump straight to it. Plus and minus, or the speed button on the banner, make play faster or slower.",
        helpPresentKeysNoChapters: "Space plays and pauses. The arrow keys step one notch. Home and End go to either end. Plus and minus, or the speed button on the banner, make play faster or slower.",
        helpPresentChapters: "Chapters are story points pinned to dates. When play reaches one, the map pauses on it, flies or cuts to its place, turns layers on or off, swaps the basemap and opens a feature if the chapter asks, and shows its title, text and picture.",
        helpPresentChaptersJump: "Play in this app moves chapter to chapter rather than one notch at a time.",
        helpPresentLoop: "When the end is reached the presentation starts over.",
        helpPresentKiosk: "Press Copy link while presenting and the link opens the app straight into the presentation. If it was playing, the link plays too. Good for a lobby screen.",
        helpStageTitle: "On stage",
        helpStageIntro: "Tools for the person at the front of the room. Each has a button on the banner and a key.",
        helpPresentGrid: "Chapter grid, or G, opens a tiled view of every chapter with a small picture of the map once it has been visited. Click a tile to jump there.",
        helpPresentSpotlight: "Spotlight, or L, darkens the map except a circle around your mouse so the room sees where you point. The arrow keys move the circle too. Press again to turn it off.",
        helpPresentInk: "Draw on the map, or D, lets you draw on the map with the mouse or a pen. Z removes the last stroke, C or Clear the drawing wipes it, and the drawing clears itself when the next chapter starts. Press D again to stop.",
        helpPresentBlack: "Black screen, or B or a full stop, blacks out the map so the room looks at you; a comma gives a white screen. Click the screen or press the key again to bring the map back.",
        helpPresentVoice: "V reads the chapter title and text aloud in the browser voice. Press V again to stop. Speaker notes are never read.",
        helpPresentPresenter: "Presenter window, or W, opens a second window with your speaker notes, what comes next, a running clock and the same buttons. Drag it to the laptop screen and put the map on the projector; the two stay in step.",
        helpPresentPace: "The presenter window keeps a clock and says whether you are ahead of, behind or on the planned length. Beside each chapter it shows how long you have spent there in this run, and once a chapter has been visited its map picture appears beside the notes and beside Up next.",
        helpPresentClean: "The map zoom buttons and compass leave while the banner is up and come back when you exit.",
        helpStoryTitle: "Making your own chapters",
